<title>UK: Fairey first-half profits rise 32 percent.</title>
<headline>Fairey first-half profits rise 32 percent.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-09-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to June 30</p>
<p>			   (million stg unless stated)</p>
<p> Shr (pence)		15.5		   vs 13.0</p>
<p> Dividend (pence)	 2.85		   vs 2.55</p>
<p> Pretax		     21.33		  vs 16.19</p>
<p> Turnover		   118.4		  vs 94.1</p>
<p>NOTE - Fairey Group Plc is an engineering company. It said in a statement that the 32 percent increase in profits and 26 percent rise in sales were achieved against a slightly more difficult market environment.  </p>
<p> Operating result	 22.06		  vs 16.73</p>
<p> Interest(payable)	0.74		   vs 0.54</p>
<p> Tax			  7.60		   vs 5.61</p>
<p> Net taxed		  13.72		  vs 10.58</p>
<p> Retained		   11.14		  vs 8.49</p>
<p> Pay date		   November 15, 1996</p>
<p> Div registration date  N/A</p>
<p> Ex-div date		N/A</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom  +44 171 542 7717</p>
